mode: "100644"
text: "# Superfans & Honest Scope\n\nThe most valuable people in any community are the small, devoted core — and the rules that keep\ncommunity-building genuine.\n\n## Superfans: find, nurture, elevate\n\nMost of a community's life comes from a **small minority of highly engaged members.** Prioritizing them\nbeats chasing broad reach.\n\n**Find them.** They're the people who interact with almost everything, reply thoughtfully, defend you\nunprompted, create about you, and show up first. (You spot them by presence over time — natively, not\nvia WoopSocial analytics.)\n\n**Nurture them.** Move them up the ladder — **lurker → regular → advocate:**\n\n- **Recognition** — name them, spotlight them, thank them publicly (with consent).\n- **Access** — early/exclusive content, a direct line, a peek behind the scenes.\n- **Status / roles** — make them moderators, ambassadors, beta testers, \"founding members.\"\n- **Collaboration** — invite them to co-create, give feedback, shape what you build.\n\n**Elevate them into advocates.** A nurtured superfan becomes a word-of-mouth engine, a UGC source, and\na moderator who helps the community run itself. A handful of true advocates outperforms a large passive\nfollowing.\n\n## Honest scope (what this is, and isn't)\n\n- **Advisory + content, not a community platform.** WoopSocial **publishes/schedules** the\n  community-building **content** (rituals, prompts, spotlights, announcements) via `scheduling-and-queue`.\n  It does **not** run Discord/Slack/groups, manage broadcast channels or an inbox, identify superfans\n  from data, track membership/retention, or show analytics. The **human runs the actual space and\n  relationships in-platform**; the **agent advises strategy and drafts/schedules the content.**\n- **No fake community — ever.** Don't buy members, run engagement pods, or astroturf activity to look\n  busy. It's **fake, detectable, and corrodes the one thing community runs on: trust.** Genuine\n  belonging is built slowly through real value and real interaction — there's no shortcut, and faking it\n  backfires.\n- **Consent & member privacy.** Get a member's **permission before spotlighting** them or reposting\n  their content; don't expose members' personal information; respect the privacy of closed spaces.\n- **It's a long-term commitment.** Community is a program you sustain (consistency > speed), not a\n  campaign you run once. Don't open a space you can't keep tending — an abandoned community is worse\n  than none.\n- **Protect the people.** Running community is real work; pair it with the boundaries in\n  `engagement-routine`, and protect the space (and yourself) per `crisis-and-moderation`.\n\n## Self-sustaining is the goal\n\nYou've succeeded when the community **doesn't need you for every interaction** — members welcome\nnewcomers, answer each other, and carry the culture themselves. Build toward handing them the keys, not\ntoward being the center of every exchange.\n"
